========================================================================================
NOTE: Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) - Asset Update Workflow
Category: IT Asset Management / Digital Asset Management (DAM)
Last Updated: October 2026
========================================================================================

1. OBJECTIVE:
   To ensure all physical, digital, or financial assets are accurately updated in the 
   system with correct metadata, valuation, status, and ownership details.

2. PREREQUISITES:
   - Proper authorization/approval from the Asset Manager.
   - Access credentials to the Asset Management System (AMS / CMDB).
   - Backup of the existing asset configuration or database record.

3. STEP-BY-STEP UPDATE PROCEDURE:
   - Step 1: Identify the target asset using its unique ID, serial number, or SKU.
   - Step 2: Verify current status (e.g., Active, In Maintenance, Deprecated, Retired).
   - Step 3: Modify relevant attributes:
     * Metadata & Description (Name, category, tags, location)
     * Technical Specs (Firmware version, capacity, hardware specs if applicable)
     * Financial Data (Current valuation, depreciation rate, cost center)
     * Ownership & Assignment (Assigned user, department, custodian)
   - Step 4: Attach supporting documents (invoice, maintenance log, compliance certificate).
   - Step 5: Save changes and submit the record for audit review.

4. IMPORTANT NOTES / BEST PRACTICES:
   - Always log the reason for the update in the audit trail (e.g., "Hardware upgrade", 
     "Reassignment to Department B", "Annual depreciation adjustment").
   - Notify the assigned custodian via email once the asset record has been successfully updated.
